  "content": {
    "id": "p56-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "State the zeroes and discontinuities of each function.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p56-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{5}{6-x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Zeroes: none. Discontinuity: $x=6$.",
          "worked": "The numerator is never zero, so there are no zeroes.\n$$\\begin{align*}6-x&=0\\\\x&=6\\end{align*}$$\nThe denominator is zero at $x=6$, so the function is discontinuous there.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 11
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{3x}{(x-1)(x-3)(x-5)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Zero: $x=0$. Discontinuities: $x=1,3,5$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x&=0\\\\x&=0\\\\(x-1)(x-3)(x-5)&=0\\\\x&=1,3,5\\end{align*}$$\nThe denominator is nonzero at $x=0$, so this is a zero. The denominator vanishes at $x=1,3,5$, with no factors cancelling, so these are the discontinuities.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x(x+1)}{(x+2)(x+3)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Zeroes: $x=0,-1$. Discontinuities: $x=-2,-3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=0,-1\\\\(x+2)(x+3)&=0\\\\x&=-2,-3\\end{align*}$$\nNeither numerator zero makes the denominator zero. No factors cancel, so the denominator zeroes give the discontinuities.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      }
    ]
  },
